"We have located the area where they are stranded, and an army helicopter is arriving to rescue them," the district's chief officer, Junu Dhakal, told PTI.

"We hope to rescue them soon." She said the group could not be called missing because officials had found the area.

Mobile phones do not work where the tourists are, Ms Dhakal said, but they are in touch with Nepal Army personnel who are posted in the national park. Officials said the names of the tourists are Moumita Halder, Piyali Koley, Jajla Trivedi Kumar, Aditya Singha, Diplina Bishwas and Rajesh De.

