The army is sending the helicopter, and the cost of the rescue will be met from Nepal's Disaster Management Fund.

Police in Dolpa had asked for a helicopter after the group could not be reached.

Authorities banned trekkers from travelling to Upper Dolpa from 29 October because of the weather, but the tourists went on despite the restriction and warnings from security personnel and their Nepali guide, Ms Dhakal said.

