They left the guide and headed towards the lake as the snow got heavier. The guide contacted the district office on Saturday evening to say the group might be stranded.

Snow has fallen continuously in Dolpa for several days, which has disrupted life in high-altitude areas and raised the risks for tourists, and the district administration has urged residents and visitors to take care.

