Nepal's weather department had warned that rain and snow were likely in the high Himalayas from Thursday night, from a weather system linked to Cyclone Arnab, which came ashore in India's Andhra Pradesh state on Wednesday.

It said parts of Karnali province, where Dolpa lies, could see snow, and the national disaster authority put the country on high alert from 29 to 31 October.

Heavy snow has stranded trekkers in Nepal at this time of year before.

Last October, snowfall from another cyclone left about 1,500 trekkers, including more than 200 foreigners, lost on buried trails in Manang district in central Nepal, and the army and police guided them to safety.
